Accumulate WindNinja phase timers across the outer "matching" loop.

W7 finding: startBuildEq/endBuildEq (ninja.cpp:407,430) and
startSolve/endSolve (:441,453) are assigned INSIDE the do/while matching
loop that closes at :491. Each outer iteration overwrites the previous
values, so the reported "Equation building time" and "Solver time" describe
only the FINAL iteration.

For domain-average initialisation the loop runs once and the numbers are
correct. For point initialisation with weather-station matching it can run
up to nMaxMatchingIters (default 150), so the printed solve time can
understate the real cost by up to that factor — which would make W7's
Amdahl answer badly wrong in exactly the case where the solve is called
most often.

This patch adds accumulators alongside the existing variables rather than
replacing them, so current output is unchanged and the new totals appear as
extra lines.

Apply with:  git -C windninja apply ../spikes/windninja-w7/accumulate-timers.patch

--- a/src/ninja/ninja.h
+++ b/src/ninja/ninja.h
@@
     double startBuildEq, endBuildEq;
     double startSolve, endSolve;
+    // W7: per-iteration timers above are overwritten by the matching loop;
+    // these accumulate across all outer iterations.
+    double totalBuildEq, totalSolve;
+    int    solveCallCount;

--- a/src/ninja/ninja.cpp
+++ b/src/ninja/ninja.cpp
@@ (each of the three constructor/reset blocks that zero the timers)
     startSolve=0.0;
     endSolve=0.0;
+    totalBuildEq=0.0;
+    totalSolve=0.0;
+    solveCallCount=0;

@@ (after endBuildEq = omp_get_wtime(); near :430)
             endBuildEq = omp_get_wtime();
+            totalBuildEq += (endBuildEq - startBuildEq);

@@ (after endSolve = omp_get_wtime(); near :453)
             endSolve = omp_get_wtime();
+            totalSolve += (endSolve - startSolve);
+            solveCallCount++;

@@ (in the timer reporting block near :583)
             input.Com->ninjaCom(ninjaComClass::ninjaNone, "Solver time was %lf seconds.",endSolve-startSolve);
+            input.Com->ninjaCom(ninjaComClass::ninjaNone, "W7 cumulative equation building time was %lf seconds.", totalBuildEq);
+            input.Com->ninjaCom(ninjaComClass::ninjaNone, "W7 cumulative solver time was %lf seconds over %d solves.", totalSolve, solveCallCount);
+            input.Com->ninjaCom(ninjaComClass::ninjaNone, "W7 matching iterations = %d", matchingIterCount);

Note: matchingIterCount is declared at :348, inside simulate_wind(), so the
last line above must sit within that function's scope — which the existing
reporting block does.
